.TH AURA-PLAYER 1 "2026" "Aura Music Player" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aura-player \- modular GPU-rendered audio player
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aura-player
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aura-player
is a modular audio player written in Go. It uses Oto as the PCM engine,
.B go-mp3
for streaming MP3 decoding and Gio for a desktop interface rendered directly
by the GPU. It does not use a WebView, HTML or JavaScript.
.PP
When one or more file paths are given on the command line, they are appended
to the queue and the first one starts playing. This allows file-manager
associations and direct playback.
.SH FORMATS
WAV, FLAC and Ogg Vorbis are decoded through the native beep adapters. MP3 is
decoded by streaming with
.BR go-mp3 .
All tracks are streamed and normalised to 48 kHz stereo PCM before entering the
audio engine, so a single queue may mix formats, mono or stereo files and
different sample rates.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/playerdoit
User skins and preferences. The active skin is preserved across upgrades and
uninstalls.
.SH OPTIONS
.B aura-player
takes no options other than audio files. Any argument is treated as a path to
add to the queue.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Juan Pablo Mu\u00f1oz Leiva (empowdered).
